{"w":2400,"h":3395,"lines":[{"c":1,"w":0.078909257253011011,"x":0.82889124299680439,"h":0.013755254666853012,"t":"Listening","y":0.11378691193032342},{"t":"SECTION 3","x":0.1769547353116008,"w":0.13374485015869139,"h":0.01472320376914027,"c":1,"y":0.15547703167303073},{"t":"Questions 21-30","y":0.15400471120651127,"c":1,"h":0.016195524146054185,"w":0.17901234944661454,"x":0.36008230368645172},{"y":0.18749999987348642,"w":0.15637860616048177,"c":1,"h":0.013081395583944722,"t":"Questions 21-25","x":0.17695472974009846},{"w":0.29629628499348959,"h":0.016195524146054185,"y":0.21937573599778049,"x":0.17901235122534614,"t":"Choose the correct letter, A, B or C.","c":1},{"x":0.17695474151439952,"y":0.24852767951629395,"t":"21 What does Trevor find interesting about the purpose of children's literature?","w":0.66255142211914064,"h":0.014553715960858749,"c":1},{"c":1,"x":0.25509075134752096,"h":0.017467026996949686,"y":0.27168816261067463,"t":"the fact that authors may not realise what values they're teaching","w":0.54127553304036446},{"y":0.28924418584512024,"t":"B","w":0.014403292338053375,"h":0.011627907185728592,"c":1,"x":0.21810699572054812},{"w":0.016460905075073223,"h":0.011627907185728592,"y":0.3037790695660505,"x":0.21810699591925348,"t":"C","c":1},{"x":0.2571524749022539,"y":0.28715096560835141,"h":0.014868491389585681,"c":1,"w":0.62151077270507815,"t":"the fact that literature can be entertaining and educational at the same time"},{"x":0.25308642749577415,"w":0.5596707661946615,"c":1,"y":0.30377906963399881,"t":"the fact that adults expect children to imitate characters in literature","h":0.014536595878106739},{"y":0.3261080136037815,"x":0.17687073860173322,"t":"22 Trevor says the module about the purpose of children's literature made him","w":0.66066375732421878,"c":1,"h":0.018109073346860294},{"t":"analyse some of the stories that his niece reads.","y":0.35174418592364032,"w":0.40329218546549472,"h":0.013096803209104779,"c":1,"x":0.25514403066883851},{"y":0.36773255794635995,"t":"B","h":0.010174418787512574,"c":1,"x":0.22016460887212561,"w":0.014403292338053375},{"t":"C","x":0.21810699593982966,"y":0.38226744161209747,"w":0.016460905075073223,"h":0.013081395583944722,"c":1},{"w":0.39729713439941405,"t":"wonder how far popularity reflects good quality.","x":0.25093881920492977,"y":0.36614044252185141,"h":0.017478419417346402,"c":1},{"x":0.25102881757022139,"y":0.38221436994233204,"t":"decide to start writing some children's stories.","h":0.013250883392226132,"w":0.38683125813802083,"c":1},{"w":0.49588475545247396,"y":0.40694935205872496,"c":1,"t":"23 Stephanie is interested in the Pictures module because","x":0.17901235466654281,"h":0.011778563015312105},{"x":0.2510288102505126,"y":0.43168433450715216,"w":0.30864196777343755,"h":0.011629619081674702,"c":1,"t":"she intends to become an illustrator."},{"t":"B","w":0.016460905075073223,"c":1,"x":0.21810699591925348,"y":0.4462209300311667,"h":0.011627907185728703},{"y":0.44611307394039423,"w":0.50205759684244788,"h":0.011778563015312216,"c":1,"t":"she can remember beautiful illustrations from her childhood.","x":0.25308642785038105},{"x":0.25102881858454701,"y":0.46075581382775876,"w":0.47736623128255201,"c":1,"h":0.013081395583944611,"t":"she believes illustrations are more important than words."},{"h":0.015659362604255822,"t":"24 Trevor and Stephanie agree that comics","x":0.17892662358149522,"y":0.48390791350107332,"w":0.37054954528808592,"c":1},{"y":0.50819321088057001,"t":"are inferior to books.","x":0.25706910227138718,"w":0.17525034586588539,"h":0.013703482732334682,"c":1},{"w":0.016460905075073223,"h":0.011627907185728703,"c":1,"x":0.21810699593982966,"t":"B","y":0.52470930210481015},{"w":0.016460905075073251,"y":0.53924418632708615,"h":0.013081394460653373,"c":1,"t":"C","x":0.2181069959192535},{"h":0.01453488398216074,"y":0.52470930218966139,"w":0.29423868815104165,"c":1,"t":"have the potential for being useful.","x":0.25102880397124855},{"c":1,"y":0.53916372175820626,"t":"discourage children from using their imagination.","w":0.40946502685546876,"h":0.013250883392226243,"x":0.25308641658184056},{"c":1,"x":0.17897108952486196,"w":0.65648666381835941,"t":"25 With regard to books aimed at only boys or only girls, Trevor was surprised","y":0.56240765506033197,"h":0.017208428489586147},{"h":0.017524013811342831,"x":0.25507148383323341,"y":0.58602292963809166,"w":0.4054873657226562,"c":1,"t":"how long the distinction had gone unquestioned."},{"h":0.011627907185728703,"w":0.014403292338053375,"t":"B","x":0.22016460885497879,"y":0.60319767421721304,"c":1},{"t":"C","w":0.016460905075073223,"h":0.013081395583944722,"c":1,"x":0.21810699593982966,"y":0.6177325578911671},{"t":"how few books were aimed at both giris and boys.","c":1,"h":0.014723203769140158,"y":0.60306242664124043,"x":0.25308641917082259,"w":0.41975308736165368},{"h":0.015552790341865852,"x":0.2550975889390435,"w":0.53098958333333335,"c":1,"y":0.61707572762077145,"t":"how many children enjoyed books intended for the opposite sex."},{"c":1,"t":"79","x":0.88271604948587612,"y":0.86918604632866725,"w":0.024691357612609877,"h":0.013081395583944722}]}